& [CoreModuleSet] is the responsibility boundary
  + [model] is versioned semantic identities, units, contexts, relations, state, instructions, package/query/result schemas, judgments, traces, effects, faults, and proof records
  + [evaluator] is one deterministic immutable-before-state to immutable-after-state transition function
  + [machine] is deterministic JSON machine form and explicitly non-cryptographic fixture content identity
  + [review] is fixture-local pertinent-history events, immutable inference capsules, and a bounded deterministic review program
  + [fixtures] is the eight CoreAcceptance programs, transitions, proof assertions, and decisions
  + [CLI] is a fixture-only list and run shell rather than the later production query protocol

& [SemanticDecisionSet] is the implemented meaning
  + [identity] is labels and aliases may address multiple units while contextual scope selects without merging
  + [inference] is conclusions preserve premises, named rule, evidence, and inferred status
  + [constraint] is missing knowledge emits unknown while a known violating value emits invalid
  + [transformation] is pure state change emits no effect
  + [effect] is denied or authorized as a pending proposal; no Core v0.1 instruction commits external change
  + [reentry] is serialized yielded state must restore exactly before control resumes
  + [surface] is verbose and condensed provenance may differ while normalized semantic IR remains equal
  + [ontology] is SKOS mapping preserves source construct, native relation, and declared fidelity

& [DeliberateLimitationSet] is retained
  + [compiler] is fixture seven accepts only its two governed surfaces
  + [digest] is fixture-only FNV-1a and grants no package authority
  + [package] is schema-only until CEB Slice 02
  + [query] is schema-only until CEB Slice 03
  + [CLI] is a fixture shell until CEB Slice 04
  + [history] is explicit no-match fixture-local review rather than database retrieval
  + [review] is deterministic harness validation rather than independent model judgment
